In article <1993Feb8.232602.25790@cs.uoregon.edu> keith@majestix.cs.uoregon.edu (Keith Steiger) writes:
>Now on to my personal gripes:
>
>Monsters have much more knowledge than they should.  For example, there was a
>level in the Dungeon of Doom with a polymorph trap on it.  I didn't think it
>too horrible, especially since I had no cat... at that point, anyway.  However,
>every monster that enters this room IMMEDIATELY dives for the polymorph trap.
>In the last case, the elf could not have seen anyone else enter the trap, and
>I was the only creature in the room capable of speech.  He polymorphed into
>a demi-lich, and my game was over.
>

Remember, those nasties have been down there an awfully long time.  Consider
the gnome whose parents grew up on that level, and their parents grew up there,
and so on, and so on...  In "reality" if you invaded someone's home, and you 
weren't the first to try it, you should expect to see organized resistance,
traps and snares, cries for help, bad guys evacuating up the stairs, more
bad guys arriving to help from other levels.  It could get ugly fast.  Yes,
obviously monsters living on those levels would know that to be a polymorph
trap, and realize that it could be turned to their benefit.

Now, if the monster is of animal or worse intelligence, I'm just raving...

>Furthermore, the monsters have total knowledge of every wand, scroll and potion
>that comes into their possession.  If I drop a wand of fire with 1 charge,
>that charge will be fired at me.  However, if I drop a wand of speed monster
>with 1 charge, they will zap themselves with it.  How could they know?  This
>bothers me no end.
>

If the monster is of below-average intelligence, I would say you have a gripe.
Remember though, that these guys grew up around wands and potions.  Monsters'
seemingly inate ability to identify wands and potions is just a simulated 
reflection of their experience in the mines, or the dungeons, or whatever.
Imagine if you had spent your whole life playing NetHack, your "identified"
list would be pretty close to complete...

Try consoling yourself with these thoughts:

